          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "Here are good, doctor-led options right along Orchard:\n\n- SW1 Clinic (Paragon) \u2013 large, full\u2011suite medical aesthetics and plastic surgery; convenient if you want many treatment types in one place. Address: 290 Orchard Road, #13-01/02/03/04/05/06, Paragon, Singapore 238859. Hours shown as Mon\u2013Fri 10am\u20138pm, Sat\u2013Sun 9am\u20134pm. ([sw1clinic.com](https://sw1clinic.com/))\n- The Chelsea Clinic (Wheelock Place) \u2013 established group practice; central and easy from Orchard MRT. Address: 501 Orchard Road, #05\u201108A, Wheelock Place, Singapore 238880. ([wheelockplacemall.com](https://wheelockplacemall.com/stores/the-chelsea-clinic/))\n- Cove Aesthetic Clinic (Wheelock Place) \u2013 boutique, doctor\u2011led clinic for lasers, injectables and facials. Address: 501 Orchard Road, Wheelock Place, #04\u201107B, Singapore 238880. ([coveaestheticclinic.com.sg](https://coveaestheticclinic.com.sg/contact/?utm_source=openai))\n- LS Aesthetic Clinic (Wisma Atria) \u2013 long\u2011running clinic right on Orchard Road; convenient for quick weekday visits. Address: 435 Orchard Road, Wisma Atria Office Tower, #10\u201104, Singapore 238877. ([lsaestheticclinic.com](https://www.lsaestheticclinic.com/contact-us/?utm_source=openai))\n- AEON Medical & Aesthetic Centre (Scotts Medical Centre, Pacific Plaza) \u2013 by\u2011appointment clinic just off Orchard; Saturday hours 10am\u20133pm listed. Address: 9 Scotts Road, Scotts Medical Centre #06\u201101/02/03, Singapore 228210. ([aeonmedical.com.sg](https://www.aeonmedical.com.sg/contact/))\n- Shiro Aesthetic Clinic (Mandarin Gallery) \u2013 aesthetics clinic within Mandarin Gallery on Orchard; good if you prefer a quieter setting. Location noted as Mandarin Gallery, 333A Orchard Road (unit shown as #03\u201135 on local listings). ([shiroaestheticclinic.com.sg](https://shiroaestheticclinic.com.sg/?utm_source=openai))\n\nQuick tips\n- Book ahead\u2014Orchard clinics fill fast on Fridays/Saturdays. As of today (Saturday, July 18, 2026), SW1 lists weekend hours till 4pm; AEON till 3pm; call to confirm slot availability. ([sw1clinic.com](https://sw1clinic.com/))\n\nIf you tell me what you want done (e.g., acne scars, pigmentation, Botox/fillers), your budget, and weekday vs weekend preference, I can narrow this to the best fit and suggest who to see first."
